Z||000000||mope||04-15-2001||06:55 PM||||HEY~<P>The power mirrors on my 86 gt dont work. So i took them off and tested them, they work. They just dont work when installed. I am guessing that the switch thingy is messed up. Could this be it or is there a bad relay or something? Inline fuse? i checked under my dash and all those fuses were ok.<P>If the switch is my problem, who has a working one they wanna sell me?<P>Thanks alot<P>mope<P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||04-15-2001||07:33 PM||||Any chance the car was owned by a smoker?  My one car was owned by a smoker and the windows worked erratically. I took the switch apart and it was full of ashes. I blew everything out and the worked fine from then on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mope||04-15-2001||07:36 PM||||he was a smoker! damnit! i just put the cenet consol all back together, i was hopping for there to be a bigger problem then just ashes!<P>thanks!!<P>mope||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||04-16-2001||04:19 PM||||The button of the power mirror switch is held onto the switch with a one way keeper mounted on a plastic piece.  It would be very easy to break if you tried to pry it off to clean the contacts underneath.  I used some spray electrical contact cleaner and worked the switch back and forth and it finally started working again.  I think the contacts just get corroded.||||reg||1
